\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  IN EUROPE - Dollar hovers, poised for breakout. \b0\par\par\uc2 590 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Mai 1999\par 17:59\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, May 20 (Reuters) - The dollar remained weaker than 125 yen and $1.06 per euro on Thursday but was likely to attack those levels in the near term, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  "The dollar could go up towards 125 yen from the 120 range that it's been stuck in recently," said Trevor Williams, senior economist at Lloyds. \par \par \uc2  "Longer term, one of two things might happen - the Japanese economy might weaken, or there will be renewed concern about the U.S. trade deficit." \par \par \uc2  The U.S. trade gap widened to a record $19.7 billion in March, but the deficit did not hurt the dollar. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was trading at 124.26/36 at 1442 GMT, from 124.36/46 in late European trade on Wednesday. Against the euro, the dollar was at $1.0617/23, from $1.0639/49 late on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The dollar remains on a strengthening path after the Federal Open Market Committee (FOMC) moved to a tightening bias on Tuesday, holding out the prize of higher U.S. interest rates and hefty U.S. yield premiums over European and Japanese debt. \par \par \uc2  "Yield spreads are moving so far in favour of the dollar, funding the trade deficit is not going to be a problem," said Michael Metcalfe, treasury analyst at NatWest Global Financial Markets. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was capped in European trade at strong resistance around 124.70 yen, traders said. But little is likely to stand in the way of a dollar move above 125 yen, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  "Clearly the Japanese authorities are not going to talk the dollar down," said Metcalfe. \par \par \uc2  Overnight comments from Japanese officials suggested the speed of any \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves was of more concern than the current level of dollar/yen, curbing market talk of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Economic Planning Agency Minister Taichi Sakaiya said the yen's recent fall had been a bit rapid but saw no problem with dollar/yen above 124. \par \par \uc2  Bank of Japan Governor Masaru Hayami said the yen decline was not excessive and he expected no big changes in the dollar/yen exchange rate. \par \par \uc2  Senior Japanese Finance Ministry official Eisuke Sakakibara was more cautious, saying he was monitoring the yen moves carefully. \par \par \uc2  Relative growth between the United States and the 11 economies of the euro zone remains a major issue for the euro/dollar rate. \par \par \uc2  A surprise fall in Germany's key sentiment survey on Thursday was a negative for the euro, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  West Germany's Ifo business climate index fell to 89.7 in April, from 90.2 in March. \par \par \uc2  "The bias is down in euro/dollar - it will go through $1.06," said Metcalfe. \par \par \uc2  Williams at Lloyds said a peaceful resolution to the conflict in Kosovo would add only one or two cents to the euro/dollar rate. \par \par \uc2  The euro was unruffled by the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's decision to leave interest rates unchanged, as expected. \par \par \uc2  Testimony by U.S. Federal Reserve Chairman Alan Greenspan offered little for traders in major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Greenspan steered clear of commenting on the U.S. economy or markets in testimony on global finance to the House Banking Committee. \par \par \uc2  The pound ended the European session softer, after UK April retail sales fell by 0.5 percent. \par \par \uc2  The pound was trading at $1.6116/26 and 65.89/94 per euro, from $1.6174/84 and 65.76/78 in late European trade on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  ((Carolyn Cohn, London Capital Markets +44 171 542 6320, carolyn.cohn@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908dv5k00jbf\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
