\par\par \b \uc2  CHRONOLOGY-Key  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2  comments by Japan officials. \b0\par\par\uc2 417 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 April 1999\par 09:18\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      TOKYO, April 28 (Reuters) - The following is a list of key \par \par \uc2  official Japanese comments and actions that have influenced \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  levels over the past year, a period in which the \par \par \uc2  dollar traded between a high of 147.20 yen last August 11 and a \par \par \uc2  low of 108.05 yen on January 11. \par \par \uc2      The dollar slipped as much as two yen briefly on Wednesday, \par \par \uc2  as Japanese officials spoke increasingly about the possibility of \par \par \uc2  extra spending to support Japan's economy. \par \par \uc2      Eisuke Sakakibara, vice finance minister for international \par \par \uc2  affairs, and \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  International Bureau chief \par \par \uc2  Haruhiko Kuroda have repeatedly said their stance at any given \par \par \uc2  time does not depend on absolute levels alone, but takes into \par \par \uc2  account changing economic conditions and market factors. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  DATE\tab     DLR/YEN OFFICIAL COMMENTS & EVENTS\par  1998  April 10\tab 128.62  Sakakibara: "Expect yen to rise."\par \tab \tab \tab      Kuroda: "Current yen weakness\par \tab \tab \tab      undesirable."\par  June 16\tab  143.24  U.S.-\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  joint dollar selling\par \tab \tab \tab      \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par  June 17\tab  136.66  Sakakibara: "\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  concern over yen fall\par \tab \tab \tab      unchanged."<\par  July 8\tab   139.40  Sakakibara: "Greatly concerned about\par \tab \tab \tab      the