\par\par \b \uc2  Ex-BOJ Kanno says  \highlight22\uc2 FX intervention \highlight\uc2  may be next step. \b0\par\par\uc2 359 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 April 1999\par 12:13\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, April 26 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  may be a suitable step should \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's economy spin further into deflation, a former Bank of Japan (BOJ) official said on Monday. \par \par \uc2  "Monetising foreign debt, or dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , could be most desirable, as it causes the least problems of moral hazard," said Masaaki Kanno, a former senior BOJ official and currently chief economist at JP Morgan in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  Moral hazard refers to the risk of prompting unrestrained government spending because of the knowledge that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would underwrite its debt. \par \par \uc2  Despite a policy decision in February by Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to guide short-term interest rates to an unprecedented zero percent, the dollar has failed to strengthen significantly against the yen. \par \par \uc2  Rather, the greenback has remained pressured against the yen due to a significant lack of risk-takers, including hedge funds and Japanese investors, to mop up excess dollars, Kanno told a press seminar. \par \par \uc2  The dollar has been supported partly by Japanese monetary authorities' verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "There is the possibility that the yen's appreciation will trigger further deflation," Kanno said. \par \par \uc2  Others have suggested that the BOJ's easy monetary stance could be underscored if the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  refrained from absorbing surplus funds through its dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , in other words, not "sterilising" the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Kanno said \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on a "massive scale" and policy coordination with the United States would be necessary for such \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to be successful. \par \par \uc2  Other possible next steps include the BOJ increasing the amount of outright JGB buying in the secondary market. \par \par \uc2  "The BOJ wants to avoid directly underwriting JGBs," Kanno said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could also provide funds to the money market by accepting commercial paper (CP), corporate bonds or even equities as collateral. \par \par \uc2  "The BOJ will likely stand vigilant to prevent serious deflation, as price stability is their key their policy objective. Deflation will hurt not only the financial sector but will also tear at the social fabric," the former central banker said. ((Tamawa Kadoya, Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3 3432 8027 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908dv4q02c5r\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
