\par\par \b \uc2  MOF paid 100 bln yen to private sector in Feb-BOJ. \b0\par\par\uc2 212 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1999\par 08:52\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, March 1 (Reuters) - Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  (MOF) paid 100.1 billion yen to the private sector in February through its special \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  account, data released by the Bank of Japan (BOJ) showed on Monday. \par \par \uc2  Redemptions of Financing Bills (FBs), which analysts said were usually the main factor behind such payments, totalled 10 billion yen in February. \par \par \uc2  Some analysts said the deviation between the two figures may mean the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  conducted small amounts of dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in February, although they did not know if the BOJ actually \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "I think the chances that the BOJ actually conducted dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  are very small, and even if they did, the amount is almost inconsequentially small," judging from the figures, said an analyst for a foreign bank. \par \par \uc2  In mid-February, Vice Finance Minister for International Affairs Eisuke Sakakibara said it was "natural" for the yen to fall as a result of the Bank of Japan's credit easing on February 12 and that he welcomed a fall in the yen. \par \par \uc2  There were no private-sector purchases of FBs in February. ((Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3 5473 3748 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010909dv3103ika\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
