\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  IN EUROPE - Dlr boosted by G7 tolerance. \b0\par\par\uc2 992 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Februar 1999\par 17:51\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Feb 22 (Reuters) - The dollar rose to a record high against the euro and a two-and-a-half month peak versus the yen on Monday amid perceptions leading industrial countries were apparently condoning a stronger U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  However, as U.S. markets opened, a flurry of profit-taking and bid withdrawal pushed the dollar to near $1.1050 per euro and 120 yen, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  "Markets earlier today saw the G7 (Group of Seven) comment on \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  as a go-ahead to buy dollars," said Tim Harris \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at National Australia Bank. "But it came off on profit-taking ahead of the Humphrey-Hawkins testimony." \par \par \uc2  Federal Reserve Chairman Alan Greenspan delivers the semi-annual Humphrey-Hawkins testimony on U.S. policy to the Senate Banking Committee Tuesday at 1500 GMT. \par \par \uc2  At 1540 GMT the euro was quoted at $1.1034/39 after falling to $1.0969 in early Monday trade, nearly eight percent lower from the peaks it traded at after its launch on January 4. \par \par \uc2  Dollar/yen was last at 120.17/22 from 122.50, the highest since December 1, 1998. \par \par \uc2  "If the appetite to buy dollars had been there, there would have very little in the way of dollar/yen in the mid-120's or euro/dollar near $1.08," Harris said. \par \par \uc2  "The Japanese have realised the damage a strong yen could do to their fragile economy. But the problem is they risk losing control either way. A dollar/yen move towards 124-125 seems to be a given, but if it goes through that level it may not stop." \par \par \uc2  Analysts said it was difficult to see \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  or the Federal Reserve \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to smooth or reverse the dollar's rise against the yen given the hands-off approach to \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets advocated by the U.S. authorities. \par \par \uc2  With regards euro weakness, Steve Barrow said the credibility of the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had been "shot down" by European politicians. \par \par \uc2  "The problem is when markets sense a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  under pressure, they tend to go for the jugular," said Barrow. \par \par \uc2  Behind negative euro sentiment is the ever-weakening euro zone economy and continuing speculation of lower interest rates despite conflicting comments from ECB officials and European politicians. \par \par \uc2  Germany's Finance Minister Oskar Lafontaine has many times in recent months called on the ECB to cut interest rates to get the euro zone economy moving and to help unemployment. \par \par \uc2  But Wim Duisenberg, ECB president told the G7 weekend meeting that current euro money policy was appropriate. \par \par \uc2  Federal Reserve Chairman Alan Greenspan delivers the semi-annual Humphrey-Hawkins testimony on U.S. policy to the Senate Banking Committee Tuesday at 1500 GMT. \par \par \uc2  At 1540 GMT the euro was quoted at $1.1034/39 after falling to $1.0969 in early Monday trade, nearly eight percent lower from the peaks it traded at after its launch on January 4. \par \par \uc2  Dollar/yen was last at 120.17/22 from 122.50, the highest since December 1, 1998. \par \par \uc2  "If the appetite to buy dollars had been there, there would have very little in the way of dollar/yen in the mid-120's or euro/dollar near $1.08," Harris said. \par \par \uc2  "The Japanese have realised the damage a strong yen could do to their fragile economy. But the problem is they risk losing control either way. A dollar/yen move towards 124-125 seems to be a given, but if it goes through that level it may not stop." \par \par \uc2  Analysts said it was difficult to see \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  or the Federal Reserve \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to smooth or reverse the dollar's rise against the yen given the hands-off approach to \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets advocated by the U.S. authorities. \par \par \uc2  With regards euro weakness, Steve Barrow said the credibility of the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had been "shot down" by European politicians. \par \par \uc2  "The problem is when markets sense a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  under pressure, they tend to go for the jugular," said Barrow. \par \par \uc2  Behind negative euro sentiment is the ever-weakening euro zone economy and continuing speculation of lower interest rates despite conflicting comments from ECB officials and European politicians. \par \par \uc2  Germany's Finance Minister Oskar Lafontaine has many times in recent months called on the ECB to cut interest rates to get the euro zone economy moving and to help unemployment. \par \par \uc2  But Wim Duisenbery, ECB president told the G7 weekend meeting that current euro money policy was appropriate. \par \par \uc2  At their Saturday meeting G7 finance ministers said nothing to indicate they would stand in the way of further dollar gains. \par \par \uc2  They also said \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  should reflect economic fundamentals and agreed to work together to avoid excess volatility and significant misalignments of exchange rates. \par \par \uc2  "The euro may bounce because no one seems to be in a hurry to stock up on the dollar just yet, but after Greenspan's speech I expect the demand to come through," Harris said. "Greenspan will present a fairly neutral picture of the U.S. economy." \par \par \uc2  Japan's top-financial diplomat, Eisuke Sakakibara, is currently of the opinion the yen should be lower, Harris said. \par \par \uc2  The Japanese are set on a course where they want to prevent government bond yields from rising above two percent before the end of the fiscal year (end-March), one trader said. \par \par \uc2  "This will add to the yen-negative scenario." \par \par \uc2  The rise in the euro's exchange rate against the yen fell short of a life-high seen on Friday. Euro/yen was last at 132.74/80 from a Monday peak at 134.80. \par \par \uc2  Broad-based dollar strength also pushed the U.S. unit to a near-six-month high versus the Swiss franc. \par \par \uc2  Dollar/Swiss was by 1644 GMT at 1.4487/97 from 1.4588, the highest level since August 31, 1998. \par \par \uc2  ((Pratima Desai, London newsroom +44 171 542 2737, pratima.desai@reuters.comm)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908dv2m041r3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
