\par\par \b \uc2  Dlr ends U.S. higher vs yen, fades vs other units. \b0\par\par\uc2 614 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Februar 1999\par 23:01\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  NEW YORK, Feb 16 (Reuters) - The dollar stretched its gains versus the yen, but slipped against most other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as they powered higher versus the slumping Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers interpreted overnight comments by Japanese officials as a green light to continue selling the yen, which fell to its lowest point in nearly two months at 118.90 per dollar. \par \par \uc2  "Most of the market had felt like if you moved dollar/yen too far too fast, you might have a Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in your face. Now that fear is gone, at least until we get to 120," said John Beerling, chief dealer at Norwest Bank. \par \par \uc2  The dollar ended higher at 118.65/70 yen, up from 118.13/23 at the open and 114.70 yen at Friday's close. The euro rose to $1.1202/07 from $1.1174/78 at the open. \par \par \uc2  The dollar's intraday rally of more than three yen on Tuesday was its biggest one-day gain in a month and pushed it to its best level since December 9, when it traded at 119.45. \par \par \uc2  The greenback stood more than four yen above its Friday New York close. U.S. trade was closed Monday for Presidents' Day. \par \par \uc2  The dollar surged overnight as Japanese officials said they expected their \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken following a cut in short-term Japanese interest rates last Friday. \par \par \uc2  Japan's top financial diplomat, Eisuke Sakakibara, told Reuters Television that the United States and other rich nations could accept a weaker yen after Japan on Friday cut a key short-term interest rate to 0.15 percent from 0.25. \par \par \uc2  "We've seen quite a bit of movement from the last U.S. session," said Beerling. "Japanese officials seem to be willing to deal with a weaker yen." \par \par \uc2  Dealers said they expect the dollar to creep toward 120 yen in coming sessions, though they noted Japanese institutions are now selling dollar-denominated assets ahead of Japan's March 31 fiscal yearend. \par \par \uc2  "There is still some caution with the yearend (Japanese) repatriation, but obviously there seems to have been a shift in policy by the Bank of Japan. I think we'll get to 120 (yen per dollar) eventually," said Ira Goldstein, a vice president at Sakura Bank Ltd. \par \par \uc2  The euro fell as low as $1.1161, its weakest level since its January 4 launch, and now stands five percent lower than its inaugural rate against the dollar. \par \par \uc2  But the euro later recovered somewhat, bolstered by its own one-percent rally against the yen. Euro/yen stalled at its recent highs near 133.15. \par \par \uc2  Most economists see European growth slowing even as the U.S. economy continues to expand at a healthy pace, which tends to boost demand for dollars. \par \par \uc2  Some economists also expect the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will soon lower interest rates, which would reduce the value of euro-denominated investments. But few observers expect the ECB to cut rates at its policy meeting on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  "You have a slowdown in Europe while the United States is still the world's growth engine. It's going to be very hard to sustain any major rally in the euro in that environment," said one dealer at a German bank. \par \par \uc2  The dollar ended lower at 1.4258/68 Swiss francs versus 1.4290/95 at the open. The British pound rose to $1.6325/35 from $1.6302/12. The greenback slipped to Canadian $1.4947/57 from C$1.5015/25. \par \par \uc2  The Australian dollar fell to $0.6340/45 from $0.6395/05. \par \par \uc2  ((-Chris Stetkiewicz, 212-859-1664)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908dv2g04f1o\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
