\par\par \b \uc2  Dollar firmer but capped by repatriation concerns. \b0\par\par\uc2 543 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Februar 1999\par 05:00\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Feb 5 (Reuters) - The dollar was slightly firmer above 112 yen at midday in Tokyo on Friday but maintained a bearish undertone on the back of market speculation of further repatriation of Japanese assets, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was quoted at 112.15/23 yen at 0301 GMT, up slightly from 111.95/00 yen in late New York on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The greenback recouped some losses from overnight and held above 112 yen for much of the morning on light short-covering and firm commercial demand by Japanese importers, which lifted the dollar as high as 112.34 yen, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  But the dollar's uptrend was blunted, dealers said, as a substantial volume of offers, said to be from U.S. operators, were seen around 112.50 yen. \par \par \uc2  "The dollar's bias will remain weak as overseas operators suspect that Japanese investors are likely to speed up repatriation of assets," said a city bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  The dollar fell overnight on rumours that Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  (MOF) had been selling U.S. Treasury bonds and urged Japanese investors to do the same before closing their books at the end of the financial year on March 31. \par \par \uc2  A MOF representative in New York denied talk that a suggestion had been made to repatriate funds to Japan before the end of the current fiscal year on March 31. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, U.S. Treasuries retained a bearish tone at midday in Tokyo following four consecutive days of declines, amid concerns about supply and rising Japanese long-term rates. \par \par \uc2  In the near term, dealers said they would focus on U.S. January non-farm jobs data at 1330 GMT for clues to direction. \par \par \uc2  "Market participants are reluctant to take fresh positions now after remarks by Japanese authorities, and they are also waiting for upcoming U.S. jobs data," said a trust bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  Economists polled by Reuters, on average, expected non-farm payrolls to rise by 135,000 in January, down from December's 378,000 rise. \par \par \uc2  Miyazawa reiterated on Friday that there were no differences between Japan and the United States over \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy. \par \par \uc2  Asked if there was any gap between the two nations regarding dollar/yen levels, he told a regular news conference: "I don't have such a sense." Asked if this meant that Japan and the United States wanted to avoid excessive rises or falls in the yen against the dollar, Miyazawa said: "That's probably correct." \par \par \uc2  Depite bearishness toward the dollar, the downside was likely to be supported by persistent concerns about possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BOJ), keeping many operators cautious about driving dollar/yen down sharply, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  They said the dollar was likely to be supported above 111.50 yen due to buying interest from Japanese importers and investors. \par \par \uc2  Elsewhere, the euro was quoted at $1.1342/46 as of 0339 GMT, compared witb $1.1333/43 in New York. \par \par \uc2  European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President Wim Duisenberg said on Thursday after an ECB governing council meeting that the ECB had left its key rates unchanged amid an outlook for stable prices. ((Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3 3432-8785 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908dv2504zc5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
