\par\par \b \uc2  Sakakibara, Miyazawa At Odds On  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Level -Report \b0\par\par\uc2 204 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Februar 1999\par 03:58\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO (Dow Jones)--There's a rift among top officials at Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  regarding how far the yen should be allowed to strengthen before authorities \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stop the move, according to a report in a Japanese monthly. \par \par \uc2  The February edition of Sentaku quotes sources as saying Vice Finance Minister for International Affairs Eisuke Sakakibara and Finance Minister Kiichi Miyazawa were at odds over the proper \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  level during the run-up to the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's dollar-buying action last month. \par \par \uc2  The sources said Sakakibara was willing to let the dollar fall to around Y105, while Miyazawa wanted to keep the dollar in the Y110-Y120 range. \par \par \uc2  The BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the dollar on January 12, buying between $3.0 billion and $4.0 billion to prop up the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . As a result, the dollar rose from around Y108.50 to Y111.00 and later built on those gains. \par \par \uc2  Ever since, the dollar has traded roughly between Y112 and Y116. \par \par \uc2  Thursday at 0250 GMT, the dollar was quoted at Y113.32, up from Y112.84 in New York late Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 04-02-99 \par \par \uc2  0258GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv2400xrt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw200\pich25\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3000\pichgoal375
