\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  IN EUROPE - Yen capped as BOJ wariness returns. \b0\par\par\uc2 653 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Februar 1999\par 11:12\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Feb 3 (Reuters) - The dollar made a steady start against the yen in Europe on Wednesday as pressure from rising Japanese government bond yields was tempered by the prospect of Bank of Japan action to curb yen gains. \par \par \uc2  Dollar/yen kept a grip on levels above 112 yen in morning trade after posting a slight recovery from a near-three week below that level in overnight dealings. \par \par \uc2  Against the euro, the dollar was on a firmer footing though shy of Tuesday's highs. Dealers said the dollar continues to find favour from the strength of the U.S. economy and rising interest rate support relative to the euro zone. \par \par \uc2  Haruhiko Kuroda, director general of the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 's International Bureau said overnight that excessive yen strength or weakness was undesirable. This reignited the prospect of Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep yen gains in check. \par \par \uc2  "People are expecting some kind \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , verbal or actual, the closer we get to 110 yen," said one UK bank dealer. "The market's pretty careful about getting too long yen anyway as support from the JGB yield story may be fairly brief." \par \par \uc2  Dollar/yen was quoted as low as 111.78 yen overnight. By 0915 GMT, it was on slightly firmer ground at 112.22/27 yen. \par \par \uc2  JGB yields rose again overnight to their highest since June 1997 amid mounting concerns of oversupply of long-term debt. \par \par \uc2  Though the rise in yields is seen benefiting the yen from the increased appeal of Japanese assets, the underlying economic outlook does not favour yen strength. \par \par \uc2  "The yen's strength on the JGB issue is probably living on borrowed time but for the moment it seems to be well entrenched," said Steve Barrow, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Bear Stearns. "There's nothing a market likes more than what it believes to be a dependable relationship which at the moment is that if JGB yields move higher the yen gets stronger." \par \par \uc2  Talk of moves for the Bank of Japan to directly underwrite government debt to tame rising JGB yields lent some support to the bond market. But analysts were wary of the long-term effectiveness of such proposals. \par \par \uc2  "BOJ purchases would help to limit a further deterioration in yield levels but would be a dramatic move away from current \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  practice elsewhere in the world," said Michael Lewis, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  economist at Deutsche Bank. \par \par \uc2  Such action has traditionally been inflationary and detrimental to the long-term prospects for the exchange rate, Lewis said. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets were relatively calm elsewhere as participants eyed the outcome of monetary policy meetings in the U.S. and Europe. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. Federal Open Market Committee ends its two-day meeting on Wednesday with most seeing interest rates on hold. \par \par \uc2  However, dealers said the bias is for higher U.S. interest rates if its robust economic growth is maintained. \par \par \uc2  This is in sharp contrast with the slowing growth prospects for the euro zone. Though the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is expected to keep rates steady at its meeting on Thursday, the market bias is for looser monetary policy in coming weeks or months. \par \par \uc2  Euro/dollar was quoted at $1.1342/47 compared with $1.1340/45 late on Tuesday in Europe. \par \par \uc2  The market was also on watch for the result of the Bank of England's two-day meeting of its Monetary Policy Meeting that starts on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  A Reuters poll of analysts points to 25 basis points being trimmed from the 6.00 percent repo rate but the outcome between that and steady interest rates is very finely balanced. \par \par \uc2  Sterling stood at $1.6368/73 and 69.38/45 pence per euro compared with $1.6443/53 and 68.94/97 pence late on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  ((Andrew Reierson, London newsroom +44 171 542 6745, uk.\b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2 .news@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908dv2305a19\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
