\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  IN EUROPE-BoJ  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  prospect caps yen. \b0\par\par\uc2 589 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Februar 1999\par 13:56\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Feb 3 (Reuters) - The yen's rally on the back of rising Japanese government bond yields was thwarted on Wednesday by the renewed prospect of Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to limit its strength. \par \par \uc2  The yen rose to its highest level in nearly three weeks in overnight trade to 111.78 to the dollar, a gain of over four percent from its lows last week. \par \par \uc2  The rally, and more importantly its relative speed, prompted Haruhiko Kuroda, director general of the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 's International Bureau, to comment on Wednesday that excessive yen strength or weakness was undesirable. \par \par \uc2  "The BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  a few weeks ago is still pretty fresh in people's minds," said one European bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  "The market is extremely sensitive to the fact the Bank of Japan is keen to clamp down on any sign of undue volatility and to maintain some \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  stability in the region as a whole." \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Japan was said to have bought dollars on January 12, lifting dollar/yen from a 28-month low of around 108 yen. \par \par \uc2  "110-120 yen is probably the favoured range by the authorities. The risk is a deeper move to 105 could open the way to the next psychological level at 100 yen," said Claudio Piron, treasury economist at Standard Chartered. \par \par \uc2  "This would be out of kilter with Japan's economic fundamentals. Exports have been slowing which are already getting a bite from yen strength." \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the renewed threat of Bank of Japan action to cap the yen was being taken seriously in the market. \par \par \uc2  By 1230 GMT, dollar/yen was trading at 112.17/22 yen. \par \par \uc2  Levels below 110 yen per dollar are seen having a negative impact on any export-led growth for Japan's struggling economy. \par \par \uc2  Meantime, moves above 120 yen could invite other countries in the region to follow the yen lower to maintain competitiveness. A weaker yen would also likely heighten the already fractious trade differences between the U.S. and \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  So far, analysts said verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  may be enough to keep a lid on the yen. \par \par \uc2  The yen's recent rally has been attributed to rising JGB yields which reached their highest level since June 1997 on Wednesday amid concerns of an oversupply of long-term debt. \par \par \uc2  Though the rise in yields is seen benefiting the yen, particularly for Japanese investors repatriating funds, the underlying economic outlook does not favour yen strength. \par \par \uc2  "The yen's strength on the JGB issue is probably living on borrowed time but for the moment it seems to be well entrenched," said Bear Stearns \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist Steve Barrow. \par \par \uc2  "There's nothing a market likes more than what it believes to be a dependable relationship which at the moment is that if JGB yields move higher the yen gets stronger." \par \par \uc2  Talk of moves for the Bank of Japan to directly underwrite government debt to tame rising JGB yields lent some support to the bond market. But analysts were wary of the long-term effectiveness of such proposals. \par \par \uc2  "BOJ purchases would help to limit a further deterioration in yield levels but would be a dramatic move away from current \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  practice elsewhere in the world," said Michael Lewis, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  economist at Deutsche Bank. \par \par \uc2  Such action has traditionally been inflationary and detrimental to the long-term prospects for the exchange rate, Lewis said. \par \par \uc2  ((Andrew Reierson, London newsroom +44 171 542 6745, uk.\b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2 .news@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908dv23059pj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
