\par\par \b \uc2  Early Europe  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2 : Euro Slightly Dn Vs Dlr, Up Vs Yen \b0\par\par\uc2 314 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Februar 1999\par 09:39\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  FRANKFURT (Dow Jones)--The euro traded a touch weaker against the dollar early Wednesday in Europe as the European \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  remains caught in a tight range ahead of the outcome of Thursday's policy-making meeting of the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The euro is, however, slightly higher against the yen despite a further uptick in Japanese bond yields, after Tuesday's sharp rise. \par \par \uc2  Around 0816 GMT, the euro was quoted at $1.1330, compared with $1.1349 around 0530 GMT in Tokyo and $1.1340 late Tuesday in New York. \par \par \uc2  The euro was also trading at Y127.35, compared with Y127.31 at 0530 GMT in Tokyo and Y127.16 late Tuesday in New York. \par \par \uc2  "With euro/dollar, attention is focused on what the ECB will or won't do on Thursday," said Alex Blinkhorn, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer at Bank of Tokyo/Mitsubishi. "If they don't reduce rates on Thursday, we may see a short breather," with the euro gaining to between $1.1450 and $1.500. \par \par \uc2  The dollar gained against the yen amid fears of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 , after earlier slipping to a three-week low during Asian trading. "The dollar is testing the Y112 level to see what the Bank of Japan will do," said Blinkhorn. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was trading at Y112.36, compared with Y112.18 at 0530 GMT in Tokyo and Y115.05 late Tuesday in New York. \par \par \uc2  A sell-off in the Japanese bond market Tuesday, and the resulting higher yields, have caused the yen to appreciate against the dollar. \par \par \uc2  Looking ahead, dealers said they expect the U.S. Federal Reserve to keep rates steady after its monetary policy committee meeting that concludes later Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  -By G. Thomas Sims; 4969 25616500; tsims@ap.org \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires  02-03-99 \par \par \uc2  0339EST \par \par \uc2  1074 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020010826dv2300842\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
