\par\par \b \uc2  BOJ Jan dlr buying estimated at $6.74 bln - bankers. \b0\par\par\uc2 208 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 Februar 1999\par 09:27\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Feb 1 (Reuters) - The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BOJ) bought an estimated $6.74 billion to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in January, bankers said on Monday. \par \par \uc2  BOJ data showed that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  (MOF) paid 1.2326 trillion yen to the private sector in January through its special \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  account. \par \par \uc2  The yen payments are a result of dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the yen by the BOJ and the maturing of financing bills (FBs) previously sold to the market by the MOF. \par \par \uc2  It paid a net 484 billion yen to the banking sector for maturing FBs, and the remaining 748.6 billion yen mostly represented the BOJ's dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , bankers said. \par \par \uc2  Bankers had estimated that the BOJ bought around $2 billion or more against the yen in the Tokyo \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on January 12, helping boost the dollar from 108.65 yen to 112.85 yen in Tokyo on that day. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's action was its first significant dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  since August 1995, when it acted in concert with the U.S. authorities. \par \par \uc2  ((Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3 3432 8027 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908dv2105d3k\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscal