\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  IN EUROPE - Dlr boosted by U.S. growth wonder. \b0\par\par\uc2 639 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Januar 1999\par 10:30\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Jan 29 (Reuters) - The dollar was up around half a percentage point versus the euro and yen in early trade on Friday, buoyed by continuing optimism about the outlook for the economy of the United States. \par \par \uc2  On the other side of the equation, weighing on the yen and the euro were the sterile prospects for economic growth in Japan and euro-zone countries, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  "The dollar is higher. There is the notion of a miracle U.S. economy running on-and-on, there is very little inflation and the stock market remains robust," said Ravi Bulchandani, head of global \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategy at Morgan Stanley. \par \par \uc2  At 0837 GMT the dollar was at 116.31/35 yen from 115.36/40 in late Europe trade on Thursday. The euro was soft just above $1.1406/10 from $1.1455/65 late Thursday. \par \par \uc2  On Thursday, the dollar set one-month highs at 116.81 yen and $1.1374 per euro. \par \par \uc2  "There is also the thinking that the U.S. economy and the stock market have the ability to shrug off the Latin American contagion," Bulchandani said. \par \par \uc2  Propping dollar/yen was a comment by Japan's top financial diplomat, Eisuke Sakakibara, who said he opposed an excessively strong or weak yen. \par \par \uc2  Sakakibara also said \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  is prepared to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stop the yen from becoming too strong. \par \par \uc2  Earlier this month, apparent \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  effectively set a floor for dollar/yen at 110. \par \par \uc2  A major economic focus on Friday are advance U.S. fourth quarter gross domestic product data due at 1330 GMT. The Dow Jones Industrial average continued its run of steady increases by picking up 0.88 percent on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  "The fall-out from Brazil was not as great as people expected, the U.S. economy is surging away," said Francis Breedon, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Lehman Brothers. \par \par \uc2  Breedon said many of the question marks hanging over the dollar were fading away. He also said the impeachment hearings against U.S. President Bill Clinton were a "red herring". \par \par \uc2  Investor withdrawal from Brazil since the beginning of this year has resulted in Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  being forced to float the real and higher interest rates around 35 percent. \par \par \uc2  "But the outflows have slowed because Brazil has said it will not impose capital controls," a trader said. "This has provided some reassurance, but it could blow up again. \par \par \uc2  The Swiss franc set near-five-month lows against the dollar at 1.4178 on Thursday as market fears about Brazil receded. \par \par \uc2  By 0857 GMT dollar/Swiss franc was higher at 1.4133/43 from 1.4070/80 late Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said markets are watching Davos in Switzerland, where Sakakibara spoke earlier, for market-moving comments by other influential central bankers and finance officials. \par \par \uc2  Other data due to be released by Eurostat at 1100 GMT on Friday are December harmonised consumer price indices for euro zone and the 15-nation European Union. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the CPI data were expected to depict a benign inflation scenario, giving the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  leeway to cut rates after their meeting next week. \par \par \uc2  "European growth has been disappointing and there is evidence of manufacturing recession," Bulchandani said. \par \par \uc2  "And the yen is going to weaken, the Bank of Japan will have no choice but to print money despite their hostility towards putting Japanese government bonds onto their books." \par \par \uc2  Senior officials in Japan's ruling Liberal Democratic Party on Friday were debating the idea of having the BoJ underwrite fresh government debt. \par \par \uc2  If adopted, this idea would necessitate creating money and in turn inflation, which eventually would erode the attraction and value of the yen, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  ((Pratima Desai, London newsroom +44 171 542 2737, pratima.desai@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908dv1t05hqg\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw200\pich25\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3000\pichgoal375
