\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  IN EUROPE - Dlr/yen weighed by trade tensions. \b0\par\par\uc2 666 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Januar 1999\par 10:52\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Jan 21 (Reuters) - Dollar/yen was offered in early European trade on Thursday worried by U.S.-Japan trade friction and comments by senior U.S. trade officials, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  U.S. Trade Representative Charlene Barshefsky said Wednesday the United States will act against Japan unless its steel exports in December show a substantial decline. \par \par \uc2  "The dollar is reacting to the growing trade tensions, particularly in the steel sector," said Nick Stamenkovic, chief European economist at Bank Austria Creditanstalt Futures. \par \par \uc2  "Growing friction on the trade front was reinforced by Barshefsky overnight." \par \par \uc2  November U.S. international trade data are due to be released at 1330 GMT. Expectations are for a deficit of $15.0 billion from a shortfall of $14.2 billion in October. \par \par \uc2  "If the trade figures come in much worse-than-expected, we could see dollar/yen trying to test 110 this afternoon," a trader said. "It's potentially a very negative number for the dollar, but in the past it has sometimes been shrugged off." \par \par \uc2  At 0843 GMT dollar/yen was quoted at 112.87/92, down nearly one yen from 113.69/74 in late European trade on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Against the euro, the dollar was offered some relief on optimism that Brazil may be starting to sort itself out. \par \par \uc2  By 0851 GMT the euro was trading around $1.1566/72 versus $1.1613/19 late Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Overnight the lower house of Brazil's Congress approved a crucial pension reform bill after several delays, signalling strong support for the government's anti-crisis austerity drive. \par \par \uc2  "The Brazil pension approval was a very positive step for all the other austerity measures needed," Stamenkovic said. "It should be a positive for the dollar." \par \par \uc2  Safe-haven flight into Swiss assets halted on the Brazil news, traders said. Dollar/Swiss franc was last at 1.3869/79, from 1.3735/45 late Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The governing council of the European \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also meets Thursday, but expectations are for no change in interest rates. "We're not expecting an ECB rate cut before March," said James McKay, chief European economist at Commonwealth Bank Australia. \par \par \uc2  A small, expected drop in the December West German IFO business climate index to 91.4 from 91.7 in November had little impact on euro levels. \par \par \uc2  But analysts took note of the Bundesbank January report which said the German economy, particularly the industrial sector, slowed significantly in late 1998. \par \par \uc2  Germany's Bundesbank also said Thursday that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to steer the direction of the euro would occur only in exceptional circumstances. \par \par \uc2  "This is more Bundesbank stuff against European political calls for \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  targets and zones," the trader said. "Trade is volatile and people are still trying to digest the speech by (U.S. Federal Reserve Chairman Alan) Greenspan yesterday". \par \par \uc2  Greenspan said it was important but not essential to keep the dollar as the world's top reserve \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and that the introduction of the euro would to some extent erode the dollar's reserve role. \par \par \uc2  The Dow, and in turn the dollar, were undermined after Greenspan said he opposed federal government investment in the U.S. stock market. \par \par \uc2  This followed an address by U.S. President Bill Clinton on Tuesday, in which he proposed much of the budget surplus in coming years should be invested in stocks. \par \par \uc2  "Greenspan said he expected the economy to slow in coming months and that he was worried about stock prices, but he didn't want to be too aggressive given the on-going Clinton impeachment trial," said McKay. \par \par \uc2  White House lawyers will wrap up Clinton's defense against impeachment charges later on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  "People want to buy the yen, but they are cautious about Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," Mckay said. \par \par \uc2  Last week apparent \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the BoJ effectively set a 110 floor for dollar/yen in the short-term, traders said. \par \par \uc2  ((Pratima Desai, London newsroom +44 171 542 2737, pratima.desai@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908dv1l061yv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
