\par\par \b \uc2  Current long-term rates not so high-BOJ's Hayami. \b0\par\par\uc2 377 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Januar 1999\par 08:56\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Jan 21 (Reuters) - Bank of Japan Governor Masaru Hayami said on Thursday that the present level of long-term interest rates in Japan was not particularly high, and a yield on the 10-year benchmark Japanese government bond below one percent was too low. \par \par \uc2  "I don't think the present long-term interest rate level is particularly high," Hayami said at a regular news conference. \par \par \uc2  He said the benchmark yield had dropped below one percent for some time since last summer, and that "interest rates below one percent were too low". \par \par \uc2  The key 203rd 10-year Japanese government bond ended Thursday trade with a yield of 1.780 percent, up one basis point from Wednesday's close. \par \par \uc2  Hayami said he was not in a position to comment on whether the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market last week to support the dollar against the yen. \par \par \uc2  Excessive movement of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and JGBs had been corrected recently, but the BOJ would closely watch their movments, he said. \par \par \uc2  In the long run, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and interest rate levels will reflect economic and price conditions, he added. \par \par \uc2  Hayami said \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was possible when the markets moved wildly and the decision to buy or sell \b \highlight22\uc2 currenccies\b0 \highlight\uc2  would be made by watching market situations. \par \par \uc2  Asked whether \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  or the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  should disclose \b \highlight22\uc2 forex intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  after a certain period, Hayami said he did not think that was necessary. \par \par \uc2  Hayami said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would need a drastic reason to purchase newly issued JGBs because it was prohibited by law from buying them, and that such a practice could hurt fiscal soundness. \par \par \uc2  But he said there was no change in the BOJ's outright bond purchase \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market. \par \par \uc2  Hayami also said: \par \par \uc2  *The amount of Japanese banks' exposure to China is bigger than that to Brazil, and could result in some impact on Japan's economy. \par \par \uc2  *The BOJ's asset quality had not been deteriorating, but there had been changes in the components of its assets as a result of BOJ efforts to support corporate finance and expansion of commercial paper (CP) \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 . ((Tokyo Newsroom +81-3 3432 8022 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908dv1l061vi\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
