\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  IN EUROPE - Dlr testing upside on Brazil hopes. \b0\par\par\uc2 679 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Januar 1999\par 11:01\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Jan 18 (Reuters) - The dollar was trading at two-week highs versus the yen in early Europe on Monday ahead of an announcement by Brazil on its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy. \par \par \uc2  "The apparently more favourable Brazilian situation seems to have given dollar/yen a boost," said Gerard Lyons, chief economist at DKB International. "Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  last week has also set a floor for the dollar/yen exchange rate." \par \par \uc2  Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President Francisco Lopes on Sunday ruled out a "centralised" exchange rate and suggested the bank may continue floating the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  when it outlines a new \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  system on Monday. \par \par \uc2  Last week's apparent \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  and comments by senior Japanese officials on inappropriate yen strength appear to have set a dollar/yen floor at 110.00, Lyons said. "It has also given the Dow a new lease of life." \par \par \uc2  On Friday the Dow Jones rose 2.41 percent to 9340.55 after Brazil made a decision to float its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  the real. The dollar was also bolstered by the higher Dow. \par \par \uc2  By 0836 GMT dollar/yen was trading near 114.75/80, the highest level since December 31, against 114.00/05 in late European trade on Friday. The euro was little changed at $1.1580/89 against $1.1593/96 late Friday. \par \par \uc2  David Bloom, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at HSBC Markets, said softer Japanese government bond prices ahead of a 20-year JGB auction on Tuesday was also supportive for dollar/yen. \par \par \uc2  The yield of the benchmark 203rd 10-year JGB was up amid expectations Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  would offer some 600 billion yen worth of JGB's with a coupon around 2.5 percent. \par \par \uc2  "The (Japan's) current account numbers also appear to be tailing off, probably because of the stronger yen," Bloom said. \par \par \uc2  Japan's November merchandise trade surplus fell 13.4 percent from a year earlier to 1.07 trillion yen, while the unadjusted current account surplus fell 5.3 percent to 1.21 trillion yen. \par \par \uc2  Traders said many early bids for the dollar were based on comments by Japan's Minister of International Trade and Industry Kaoru Yosano on U.S.-Japan trade friction. \par \par \uc2  Yosano said the row over surging Japanese steel exports to the United States will subside this year as U.S. steel demand decreases rapidly. \par \par \uc2  Japanese Prime Minister Kiichi Miyazawa saying it would be very hard to suspend the five percent consumption tax was also undermining the yen, analysts said. Miyazawa also said he expects the "direction" of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market stability measures to be fleshed out at the G7 June meeting in Cologne. \par \par \uc2  A U.S. holiday on Monday may be the first of several days of volatile low volume trade, traders said. \par \par \uc2  Federal Reserve Chairman Alan Greenspan's testimony on the state of the economy before the House Ways and Means Committee on Wednesday will keep volumes subdued, they added. \par \par \uc2  Ongoing concerns are the health of Russian President Boris Yeltsin and the U.S. Senate impeachment trial of U.S. President Bill Clinton. \par \par \uc2  White House lawyers will begin presenting their defense on Tuesday, the same day the president is expected to give his State of the Union address to Congress. \par \par \uc2  The apparent calm in Brazilian markets also appears to have briefly arrested Swiss franc gains versus the dollar. \par \par \uc2  By 0913 GMT, dollar/Swiss franc was at 1.3831/36 from 1.3767/77 in late Europe on Friday, while euro/Swiss franc was quoted around 1.6020/25 versus 1.5965/70. \par \par \uc2  Bundesbank council member Hans-Juergen Krupp attends a new year reception at the state of Hamburg's local \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , while Wim Duisenberg, head of the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , is expected to deliver a speech at an Euro-11 meeting this later on Monday. \par \par \uc2  U.S. Deputy Treasury Secretary Lawrence Summers has postponed a visit to Japan and other Asian countries this week. ((Pratima Desai, London newsroom +44 171 542 2737, pratima.desai@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908dv1i06bhe\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
