\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2  Govt, BOJ Study Yen-Euro  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Issue -Nikkei \b0\par\par\uc2 215 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Januar 1999\par 07:48\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par TOKYO (Dow Jones)--The Japanese government, in conjunction with the\par Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , is considering laying the groundwork for \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in case of sharp swings in the yen-euro exchange rate, the\par Nihon Keizai Shimbun Saturday morning edition reports.\par    Anticipating that the euro will occupy a central position alongside\par the dollar in global markets, Japan's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  authorities have\par concluded they must widen the scope of their market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to\par include the new common \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par    To that end, the BOJ is holding discussions with the European\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  - the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  for the euro zone - and central banks\par of zone member countries. The institutions are weighing the\par establishment of a system under which central banks could lend each\par other euro-denominated funds for market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par    The BOJ currently lacks the euro-denominated reserves necessary for\par a sustained \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to prop up the yen against the new \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    Within the Japanese government and the BOJ, fears are mounting the\par yen will grow vulnerable to volatility, caught in an unstable position\par between the dollar and euro poles.\par    The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  now believes it must be ready to stage \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par to check volatile swings in the yen-euro rate.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires 16-01-99\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 0648GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv1g00dfc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
