\par\par \b \uc2  Tokyo Stocks Shrug Off Brazil, End Sharply Up On Weak Yen \b0\par\par\uc2 322 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Januar 1999\par 07:57\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO (Dow Jones)--In sharp contrast to other Asian markets, the Tokyo stock market shrugged off Brazil's financial crisis Thursday and gained strongly as it focused instead on weakness of the yen. \par \par \uc2  The Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  slid against the dollar, trading at Y113.40 in Tokyo late Thursday against Y113.13 in New York late Wednesday, and this encouraged buying in shares of exporters which had been hit by the yen's recent strength. \par \par \uc2  "I think people are reluctant to bet against \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Richard Jerram, chief economist at ING Baring Securities. He said that following Tuesday's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to push down the yen, the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  could drop further. \par \par \uc2  In addition, some traders said they were encouraged by Wall Street's relative strength in the face of the Brazilian crisis. Although the Dow Jones Industrial Average fell 1.3% Wednesday, it closed well off its lows, and a rise in Standard & Poor's March stock futures in Asian screen trade Thursday -- they stood at 1,248.70 points at 0630 GMT, up 9.70 -- implied that Wall Street could continue rebounding when it reopened. That could help Tokyo, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The Nikkei average of 225 selected issues surged 335.26 points or 2.5% to 13,738.86, while the broader Tokyo Stock Price Index closed 12.86 points or 1.2% up at 1,069.94. \par \par \uc2  Volume was estimated at a moderate 393 million shares compared to 375.5 million Wednesday. Traders said some investors were out of the market ahead of a national holiday in Japan Friday, when the exchange will be closed. \par \par \uc2  Major technology names put on solid gains, including Sony, which rose Y90 or 1.2% to 7,650 for a second straight gain after nine consecutive daily losses. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 14-01-99 \par \par \uc2  0657GMT \par \par \uc2  4159 5011 55117 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv1e00b0r\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
