\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Options: Yen Volatilities Dn, Spot Dlr Locked In Y113s \b0\par\par\uc2 421 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Januar 1999\par 05:58\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO (Dow Jones)--Volatilities implied by Japanese yen \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  options are lower in Tokyo Thursday compared with their levels in New York late Wednesday, as spot dollar trading calmed down, staying in the Y113s Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Euro options are up compared to New York. \par \par \uc2  Yen volatilities went up Wednesday on news that Brazil had effectively devalued its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , spurring fears among some that the turmoil could affect U.S. equities and the U.S. economy, which caused dollar sales. \par \par \uc2  But they have eased partly due to the spot dollar being sandwiched between Y113.01 and Y113.75, as the market tries to figure out what effect Brazil's crisis will have on the dollar. Other market players say that there could be a contagion effect from Latin America, with the turmoil coming back to Asia and therefore affecting Japan and undermining the yen. \par \par \uc2  Additionally, players are reluctant to take aggressive positions ahead of the holiday in Japan Friday and the U.S. Monday, or to push the bottom of the dollar's range, as Tuesday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  is still fresh in their minds. \par \par \uc2  "The (spot) dollar is capped and it's hard to push down because of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  fears. It's locked in a range in the Y113s, which has pushed volatilities down," said a Japanese bank trader. \par \par \uc2  In the over-the-counter market, one-month at-the-money dollar/yen options imply volatility of 18.95% bid, down from 19.5% in New York Wednesday, and below 19.1% in Tokyo Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Against the euro, they are higher at 10.85%, from 10.7% in New York Wednesday. Euro/dollar options were quoted at 9.7% in Tokyo Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief Gustavo Franco resigned Wednesday and his successor, Francisco Lopes, announced a widening of the trading band for the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the real. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  immediately plunged 8.2% to BRR1.32 to the dollar, the floor of the new expanded trading band. \par \par \uc2  At 0440 GMT, the dollar is at Y113.41, up from Y113.13 late Wednesday in New York. The euro is at $1.1642, down from $1.1663 Wednesday in New York. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Risk-reversals favor dollar put options against the Japanese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ,\par dealers said. Risk-reversals measure the market preference for either\par put or call options by the premium or discount applied.\par    -By James Simms, 813-5255-2940; jsimms@ap.org\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires 14-01-99\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 0458GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1077 4127 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv1e00ax2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
