\par\par \b \uc2  Sony Shrs Continue Rebound;  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Larger Factor Than Brazil \b0\par\par\uc2 240 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Januar 1999\par 03:22\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO (Nikkei/Dow Jones)--Sony Corp. (SNE or 6758) shares are higher midday Thursday after beginning to rebound Wednesday from a nine-day slide caused by earnings worries related to yen strengthening. \par \par \uc2  Sony shares opened the day Y40 below Wednesday's close at Y7,520 on the overnight drop in New York, where the Dow Jones Industrial Average lost 125.12 points to 9349.56. U.S. equities fell after the president of Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  resigned and his successor announced a widening in the trading band for the real, Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The news triggered worries of a new crisis in emerging markets. \par \par \uc2  While that news hurt U.S. stock prices, some traders said it is less of a factor for Japanese markets, and that it only hurts Sony in so far as it contributes to a slowdown in the U.S. \par \par \uc2  After initial sell orders for Sony were through, players resumed buying, encouraged by the fact that the dollar has remained steady against the yen since the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  In addition, the ability of U.S. high-technology stocks to ride out the DJIA's fall relatively well also supported sentiment for Sony, one dealer said. \par \par \uc2  At midday, Sony is up Y120 at Y7,680. Volume in the morning totaled 822,700 shares. \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 14-01-99 \par \par \uc2  0222GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv1e00arp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*