\par\par \b \uc2  Early Tokyo: Dollar Up A Bit Vs Yen; Brazil A Mixed Factor \b0\par\par\uc2 326 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Januar 1999\par 01:41\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO (Dow Jones)--The dollar is slightly higher against the yen in early Tokyo trading Thursday, but trading was quiet and directionless as players concluded that overnight news out of Brazil had mixed implications for the yen. \par \par \uc2  The euro is higher against the dollar. \par \par \uc2  Global markets were rattled Wednesday when Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  president Gustavo Franco resigned and was replaced by Francisco Lopes, who quickly announced that Brazil would widen the dollar's trading band for the real (BRR) to BRR1.20-1.32 from BRR1.12-1.22. \par \par \uc2  Traders in Tokyo said that while the news was dollar-negative if turmoil in Latin American markets weighed on U.S. asset prices, the market would be reluctant to sell dollars too aggressively after the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  In addition, some traders said that the instability in Latin American financial markets could spread to Asia, putting downside pressure on the yen. But most traders said fresh factors were needed to push the dollar up further against the yen. \par \par \uc2  "It doesn't seem like the dollar will rise rapidly," said Yukihiko Hashimoto, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  manager at Sanwa Bank in Tokyo. "The Brazilian situation hasn't been resolved yet." \par \par \uc2  Traders said talk that Japanese exporters had placed big orders to sell dollars was weighing on the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's upside. \par \par \uc2  Around 0030 GMT (7:30 p.m. EST Wednesday), the dollar was trading at Y113.15, down from Y113.27 around 0001 GMT but above Y113.13 in New York late Wednesday. The dollar was quoted at Y112.45 late in Tokyo Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The euro was trading at $1.1685, a little below 1.1689 earlier but above $1.1663 late Wednesday in New York. The euro was at $1.1561 in Tokyo late Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 14-01-99 \par \par \uc2  0041GMT \par \par \uc2  1074 1863 4162 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv1e00ao7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
