\par\par \b \uc2  Dollar edges up vs yen in Tokyo on Brazil jitters. \b0\par\par\uc2 606 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Januar 1999\par 06:28\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      TOKYO, Jan 14 (Reuters) - The dollar was slightly higher \par \par \uc2  against the yen by midday Tokyo on Thursday as Brazil's \par \par \uc2  effective devaluation raised speculation that financial turmoil \par \par \uc2  may spread to Asia, dealers said. \par \par \uc2      Commercial demand ahead of a three-day holiday in Japan and \par \par \uc2  weakness in Japan's banking shares also underpinned the \par \par \uc2  greenback, dealers said. \par \par \uc2       While dealers remain wary of possible Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the dollar's newfound bullishness may be limited, \par \par \uc2  dealers said. \par \par \uc2      The dollar saw steady profit-taking and sporadic sales by \par \par \uc2  Japanese exporters near highs, dealers said. \par \par \uc2      Economic Planning Agency chief Taichi Sakaiya said on \par \par \uc2  Thursday the dollar/yen \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  level was now in an "acceptable \par \par \uc2  range" for most Japanese firms after the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "Sakaiya's remarks blunted the dollar's upside," a dealer at \par \par \uc2  a trust bank said. On Wednesday, Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  widened its real-dollar \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  band to allow the \par \par \uc2  Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to trade at between 1.2 and 1.32 reais from \par \par \uc2  1.22 against the dollar. \par \par \uc2  The de facto devaluation raised concerns over new \par \par \uc2  speculative attacks on Asia's regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , such as the \par \par \uc2  Hong Kong dollar. \par \par \uc2      But some dealers said the impact on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market may \par \par \uc2  be limited. \par \par \uc2      "Brazil has been a worry since last year. Since the \par \par \uc2  financial turmoil in October, I think a lot of short-term \par \par \uc2  positions have been cleared out," a dealer at an European bank \par \par \uc2  said. \par \par \uc2  He added: "There are fewer speculative players in the \par \par \uc2  market. Lack of liquidity in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets will likely reduce \par \par \uc2  the impact of sharp fluctuations in the stock and bond markets." \par \par \uc2  Finance Minister Kiichi Miyazawa said on Thursday he \par \par \uc2  believed the Group of Seven (G7) and the International Monetary \par \par \uc2  Fund would be able to cope with the Brazilian crisis because \par \par \uc2  they were now used to dealing with such crises. \par \par \uc2      He said he believed Brazil and the IMF could reach agreement \par \par \uc2  so that the crisis did not spread. \par \par \uc2      Elsewhere, the euro was slightly lower against the dollar. \par \par \uc2  As of 0403 GMT, the euro stood at $1.1638/48. \par \par \uc2      The euro lost ground against the yen on profit-taking, \par \par \uc2  dealers said. \par \par \uc2      "There's good two-way interest in euro/yen, with decent \par \par \uc2  volume," a dealer at another city bank said. \par \par \uc2      The yen's overnight fall against other major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  was \par \par \uc2  triggered by aggressive euro buy-backs against the yen by U.S. \par \par \uc2  fund operators. \par \par \uc2      The euro stood at 131.99/2.15 yen compared with 132.09 yen \par \par \uc2  in late New York on Wednesday.     Dealers expect trade to \par \par \uc2  remain lacklustre ahead of the long weekend in Japan, a holiday \par \par \uc2  in New York on Monday and key financial meetings over the \par \par \uc2  weekend. \par \par \uc2  Miyazawa will depart Thursday afternoon to attend the \par \par \uc2  two-day Asia-Europe Meeting (ASEM) that begins in Frankfurt on \par \par \uc2  Friday. \par \par \uc2      Deputy finance ministers of the G7 will also meet in \par \par \uc2  Frankfurt on Saturday. \par \par \uc2      "The markets will be closely watching how overseas markets \par \par \uc2  react to Brazil's devaluation. But trade will likely pick up in \par \par \uc2  earnest after Tuesday," the European bank dealer said.     The \par \par \uc2  dollar stood at 113.15/25 yen and the euro was at $1.1666/71 in \par \par \uc2  late New York on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2      The markets shrugged off news that Japan's ruling Liberal \par \par \uc2  Democratic Party (LDP) and small Liberal Party had agreed on \par \par \uc2  Wednesday to form a coalition. \par \par \uc2      Prime Minister Keizo Obuchi was scheduled to hold a news \par \par \uc2  conference on the cabinet reshuffle at 4 p.m. (0700 GMT). \par \par \uc2  ((Tamawa Kadoya, Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3 3432 8027 \par \par \uc2  tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908dv1e06mm9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
