\par\par \b \uc2  U.S. Tsys Dn Late In Tokyo On Pft Taking; 30-Yr Dn 14/32 \b0\par\par\uc2 375 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Januar 1999\par 07:47\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO (Dow Jones)--U.S. Treasurys were sold across the yield curve Thursday in Tokyo, with local investors viewing the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's strength and gains in New York as a signal to trim dollar-denominated assets. \par \par \uc2  "Investors trading in Tokyo are still predominantly sellers," said one trader at a Japanese bank. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Traders said they couldn't be sure if investors were selling Treasurys\par to bolster earnings in preparation for Japan's March 31 fiscal-year end,\par or if they were selling dollar assets because they expect the dollar to\par be hurt by the close financial ties between the U.S. and Brazil.\par    4 5/8%   2-year 100        Dn  4/32  4.62%\par    4 1/4%   5-year  98 14/32  Dn  5/32  4.61%\par    4 3/4%  10-year 100  4/32  Dn  3/32  4.73%\par    5 1/4%  30-year 101  9/32  Dn 14/32  5.17%\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 2-30-Yr Yield Spread: 55 BPS Vs 58 BPS\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par At the Chicago Board of Trade, March bond futures were at 125-31, down\par 2/32 from Wednesday. The March Eurodollar contract on the Singapore\par International Monetary Exchange was at 95.045, down from 95.075\par Wednesday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The flight to the perceived safe-haven of U.S. bonds that occurred\par following news Wednesday of Brazilian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  President Gustavo\par Franco's resignation and the effective devaluation of the Brazilian real\par also gave investors a chance to book profits, traders said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "In general, there's been more selling in the short end, which is a\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  play," said another trader.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par A few traders speculated that Treasurys are also weaker since the Bank\par of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's decision Tuesday to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets and cap\par the yen's strength isn't likely to stave off dollar weakness for long.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Around 0613 GMT, the dollar was trading at Y113.35, up from Y113.13 in\par New York late Wednesday. The dollar was quoted at Y112.45 late Wednesday\par in Tokyo.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Japanese markets will close Friday for a holiday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -By Kenji Hall, 813-5255-2939, khall@ap.org\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires  01-14-99\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 0147EST\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1079 4041 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020010826dv1e003dk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
