\par\par \b \uc2  Dlr stuck in lacklustre Tokyo trade, wary of BOJ. \b0\par\par\uc2 531 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Januar 1999\par 07:48\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     0618 GMT\tab  TRADED HIGH/LOW AS OF 0600 GMT\par  USD/JPY     112.34/39\tab \tab 112.80-112.22\par  EUR/USD     1.1556/61\tab \tab 1.1576-1.1555\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  ---------------------------------------------------------------\par \f28 \par \par \uc2      TOKYO, Jan 13 (Reuters) - The dollar was stuck in a tight \par \par \uc2  range by late Tokyo on Wednesday as many dealers stayed on the \par \par \uc2  sidelines, remaining wary after apparent Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BOJ) \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Tuesday, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Short-covering and commercial demand pushed the dollar higher \par \par \uc2  in early trade, but the greenback found strong resistance around \par \par \uc2  highs on offers from U.S. fund operators and Japanese exporters. \par \par \uc2  Offers from U.S. fund operators were detected around 112.80 yen, which was also the level to which the dollar rebounded after BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Tuesday, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Sporadic sales from Japanese exporters also limited the upside, they said. \par \par \uc2  "The BOJ action blunted the drive to send the dollar lower, but bearish sentiment does not change much after one attempt," a dealer at a major city bank said. \par \par \uc2  "It may take some time, but the markets will likely try for 110 yen and test the resolve of the monetary authorities," the bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  On Tuesday, the BOJ showed its determination to check the yen's surge against the dollar, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy the U.S \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  below 110 yen, bankers said. \par \par \uc2  The BOJ likely bought around $2 billion or more against the yen in the Tokyo market on Tuesday, bankers said on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's action on Tuesday was its first since it conducted a number of dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in 1996, while the last significant dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was in August 1995, when it acted in concert with U.S. authorities. \par \par \uc2  U.S. Treasury Secretary Robert Rubin repeated on Tuesday that he favored a strong dollar. He declined to comment on specific levels. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the near-term focus would continue to be the outlook for the U.S. economy and equities, and Latin America. \par \par \uc2  U.S. Federal Reserve Vice Chairwoman Alice Rivin on Tuesday said stock market prices were high and future corporate earnings were likely to be a disappointment. \par \par \uc2  When queried about her outlook for U.S. corporate earnings in the near future, she said in an interview on CNN's Moneyline program: "All the signs point to somewhat disappointing earnings as we move ahead." \par \par \uc2  The Dow Jones Industrial Average closed down 145.21 points at 9,474.68 in New York on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Rising U.S.-Japan trade tensions are also expected to keep pressure on the dollar, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  U.S. Trade Representative Charlene Barshefsky, after meeting with Japanese Trade Minister Kaoru Yosano, said the United States would not tolerate unfair practices in the steel or any other market. She also said that trade tensions "are increasing, quite dramatically". \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, Rubin insisted that the dollar should not be used as a tool in the nation's trade policy. \par \par \uc2  The dollar stood at 112.38/43 yen and the euro was at $1.1572/80 in late New York on Tuesday. ((Tamawa Kadoya, Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3 3432 8027 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908dv1d06q3j\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
