\par\par \b \uc2  JGBs end higher but lose momentum after auction. \b0\par\par\uc2 494 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Januar 1999\par 08:04\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Jan 13 (Reuters) - Cash and futures Japanese government bonds (JGBs) ended firmer on Wednesday, but lost momentum in a quiet afternoon session in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  Traders said most gains were made in morning trade in response to overnight gains on LIFFE. \par \par \uc2  "The market seemed to be taking a breath in the afternoon session after seeing active investor action in the six-year JGB auction (on Tuesday)," said a trader at a Japanese trust bank's securities unit. \par \par \uc2  Yield of the benchmark 203rd 10-year JGB was down four basis points at 1.730 percent as of 0615 GMT. \par \par \uc2  Key March 10-year JGB futures ended the day at 130.80 percent compared to Tuesday's finish of 130.38. Turnover was a sparse 32,882 lots. \par \par \uc2  But JGB's rise was limited as market speculated there could be profit taking if March futures climbed to around 131, traders said. \par \par \uc2  For March, there is minor resistance at 131.10-131.20 and support at 129.70, they said. \par \par \uc2  "Where we are now is very comfortable and the market is basically in a wait-to-see mood amid a lack of market incentives," said a Japanese bank trader. \par \par \uc2  Another impediment to further JGB gains is pending longer-end JGB auctions, traders said. \par \par \uc2  "The JGB market is now obsessed with the issue of oversupply. As long as there are auctions, volatile trade will continue," the trader said. \par \par \uc2  The market expects a 20-year JGB auction on January 19, the same day as a BOJ Policy Board meeting is scheduled, both traders said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  (MOF) said it would offer three-month Treasury bills through price-competitive auctions on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Volume is expected to be two trillion yen, traders said. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, some traders said the JGB market will gradually calm after Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BOJ)'s dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  "BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  means they want to avoid higher interest rate which was part of reasons for higher yen. That was one of the reasons why market was releaved today," said a trader at a Japanese fund management firm. \par \par \uc2  Key June three-month euroyen futures were settled at 99.43, up one tick from Tuesday's 99.42. Turnover was a sparse 20,083 lots. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the euroyen market was benefiting possibly from the BOJ's dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  On Tuesday, the BOJ was estimated to have bought $2 billion from the Tokyo \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in an attempt to prop up the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which had taken a 7.5 percent dive in the new year against the yen. \par \par \uc2  The key overnight rate was at around 0.23 percent in afternoon session, compared with Tuesday's weighted average of 0.22 percent. \par \par \uc2  The market will be closed on Friday for a Japanese national holiday. \par \par \uc2  ((Mariko Hayashibara, Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3 3432 8676 \par \par \uc2  tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908dv1d06q34\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
