\par\par \b \uc2  Dollar/yen boxed by Tokyo midday on caution on BOJ. \b0\par\par\uc2 724 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Januar 1999\par 06:50\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      TOKYO, Jan 13 (Reuters) - The dollar fluctuated in a boxed \par \par \uc2  range against the yen by Tokyo midday on Wednesday as the market \par \par \uc2  remained careful about building up fresh positions heavily as \par \par \uc2  caution over possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BOJ) \par \par \uc2  persisted. \par \par \uc2      Early rounds of short-covering and commercial demand pushed \par \par \uc2  up the dollar, but it found strong resistance around the high \par \par \uc2  amid offers by U.S. fund operators and Japanese exporters. \par \par \uc2      "The dollar is still under strong selling pressure on its \par \par \uc2  rallies particularly around 113 yen, but at the same time the \par \par \uc2  market was wary about selling the dollar aggressively after \par \par \uc2  yesterday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," a U.S. bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2      "I feel the market will gradually test the dollar downwards \par \par \uc2  again as more dollar-selling incentives surface in the market. \par \par \uc2  Still, the market will be more careful about hammering it down \par \par \uc2  aggressively below 110 yen." \par \par \uc2      Early rounds of commercial bids pushed up the dollar, but \par \par \uc2  hit a resistance around 112.80 yen, which was also a level that \par \par \uc2  the dollar rebounded after the BOJ's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2      On Tuesday, the BOJ showed its determination to check the \par \par \uc2  yen's surge against the dollar, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy the U.S. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  below 110 yen, bankers said. \par \par \uc2      The BOJ likely bought around $2 billion or more against the \par \par \uc2  yen in the Tokyo market on Tuesday, bankers said on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2      The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's action on Tuesday was its first since it \par \par \uc2  conducted a number of dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in 1996, while \par \par \uc2  the last significant dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was in August \par \par \uc2  1995, when it acted in concert with U.S. authorities. \par \par \uc2  Despite the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , sentiment towards the dollar \par \par \uc2  stayed weak as the market continued to focus on dollar-bearish \par \par \uc2  factors. \par \par \uc2  Concerns over the outlook of the U.S. stock market were \par \par \uc2  starting to heat up again reflecting overnight falls in \par \par \uc2  Brazilian share prices and growing pessimism over the situation \par \par \uc2  in Latin America, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  In Brazil, where a large state recently imposed a debt \par \par \uc2  moratorium and the government is embroiled in a fight about tax \par \par \uc2  hikes, the stock market tumbled by more than seven percent. \par \par \uc2      In Mexico, the peso fell substantially as Mexican markets \par \par \uc2  slumped amid fears over deepening losses in Brazilian shares. \par \par \uc2      The Dow Jones Industrial average was down 145.21 points or \par \par \uc2  1.5 percent to 9,474.68 at the close on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2      Alice Rivlin, vice chairwoman of the Federal Reserve Board, \par \par \uc2  on Tuesday said stock market prices are high and future \par \par \uc2  corporate earnings are likely to be a disappointment. \par \par \uc2      In an interview on CNN's Moneyline programme, Rivlin said: \par \par \uc2  "Prices in the stock market are clearly very high. You have to \par \par \uc2  be very optimistic about earnings to justify those prices, but \par \par \uc2  that's been true for a while." \par \par \uc2  Dealers said they would focus on developments in the equity \par \par \uc2  market in order to determine trends of the dollar, but many \par \par \uc2  operators were still eager to sell the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on rallies \par \par \uc2  against the yen. \par \par \uc2  "There are relatively strong offers by U.S. fund operators, \par \par \uc2  Japanese life insurers and exporters lined up above 113 yen. \par \par \uc2  Unless the dollar convincingly breaks through 113.50 yen, the \par \par \uc2  dollar's basic trend should remain weak," another dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said active profit-taking demand by U.S. fund \par \par \uc2  operators in euro/yen also indirectly weighed on the dollar's \par \par \uc2  topside against the yen. \par \par \uc2      The euro stood around 130 yen, but its topside was \par \par \uc2  completely blocked throughout morning trade, they said. \par \par \uc2      As of 0346 GMT, the euro stood 129.98/130.18 yen compared \par \par \uc2  with 130.12 in late New York trade on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2      Vice Finance Minister Koji Tanami declined comment on \par \par \uc2  Wednesday on any possible \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \par \par \uc2  authorities but said market volatility was undesirable. \par \par \uc2      Asked if he welcomed the dollar's subsequent four yen \par \par \uc2  rebound, Tanami repeated that he could not comment directly, but \par \par \uc2  added: "As the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market is widely used for \par \par \uc2  economic transactions, very volatile movements are undesirable." \par \par \uc2  But the market's reaction to his comments was limited. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was at 112.38/43 yen and the euro was at \par \par \uc2  $1.1572/80 in late New York on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  ((Chikafumi Hodo, Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3 3432-8785 \par \par \uc2  tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908dv1d06q26\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
