\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  changed dlr/yen trend-LDP's Shiozaki. \b0\par\par\uc2 287 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Januar 1999\par 04:52\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Jan 13 (Reuters) - The rising trend of the yen has changed following the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, reversing a misguided strong-yen policy of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 , a prominent ruling party politician said on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  "It seems that the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  yesterday, and I think the trend has changed from a stronger yen to a bit weaker yen, compared to when we had 108 yen," the Liberal Democratic Party's (LDP) Yasuhisa Shiozaki told Reuters Television in an interview. \par \par \uc2  Shiozaki, a one-time BOJ bureaucrat who was parliamentary vice finance minister in the previous government of Ryutaro Hashimoto, is active in LDP financial and economic policy-making. \par \par \uc2  Bankers said the BOJ appeared to have sold yen and bought $2 billion or more on Tuesday, hoisting the dollar up from around 108 yen to its present level around 112 yen. \par \par \uc2  "At this time, I think we shouldn't have a stronger yen, because of weakness in the economy," Shiozaki said. \par \par \uc2  "I don't think there is any consensus of having a stronger yen in political circles, but somehow, so far we have had the trend of going towards a strong yen, probably initiated by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," he said. "I think that was the wrong direction." \par \par \uc2  Japan must be concerned about trade friction, which can be exacerbated by a weak yen-induced surge in Japanese exports, he said. "But in the longer term, probably even the Americans would appreciate a stronger Japanese economy." \par \par \uc2  Shiozaki said it was possible the government could compile a supplementary budget in the latter half of thel: tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908dv1d06pnm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
