\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2  Debt/Ends -2: Bonds Not Impacted By BOJ  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 278 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Januar 1999\par 08:47\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Traders said \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's move to cap the yen's strength against the dollar in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets had no noticeable impact on bond market activity, although some traders said the recent sharp rise in yields was in part responsible for the yen's rise. Tuesday, the Bank of Japan bought an estimated $1 billion to $3 billion in exchange for yen, sending the dollar shooting up to around Y112.46 late in New York, from Y108.72 Monday. \par \par \uc2  In the money market, the Bank of Japan took a neutral stance - as traders had predicted. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  drained all excess funds during its 0020 GMT Wednesday (7:20 p.m. EST Tuesday) \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the first time since Dec. 14. The Bank of Japan has kept reserves roughly Y100 billion below the requirement for the past four sessions. \par \par \uc2  The key unsecured overnight rate was around 0.21% late Wednesday, well below the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's target rate of 0.25%. That was down from 0.25% before the morning \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and lower than Tuesday's weighted average rate of 0.22%. \par \par \uc2  In the corporate bond market, Mitsui & Co. launched a total Y25 billion of bonds in two tranches. Y15 billion 2.1% seven-year bonds were sold via lead manager Sakura Securities, and Y10 billion of 2.52% 10-year bonds were offered through Fuji Securities. \par \par \uc2  Shinko Industries Co. offered Y10 billion of 2.66% seven-year bonds through lead manager Nikko Securities. Tokyo Electric Power launched Y50 billion of 2.7% 20-year bonds through Daiwa Securities. \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires  01-13-99 \par \par \uc2  0247EST \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020010826dv1d002kp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
