\par\par \b \uc2  BOJ  \highlight22\uc2 Intervenes \highlight\uc2 /Nikkei -2:  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Prompts Some Selling \b0\par\par\uc2 188 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Januar 1999\par 15:01\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO (Nikkei)--The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market Tuesday morning and afternoon, buying about $2 billion in its first effort to stem yen appreciation in 35 months, The Nihon Keizai Shimbun reported in its Wednesday morning edition. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  prompted some selling of yen for dollars, boosting the greenback by as much as Y4 to above Y112.50. \par \par \uc2  The BOJ first \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  at about 10 a.m. local time (0100 GMT), sending the dollar on a quick rise from below Y109 to above Y111.50. Shortly after 4 p.m. (0700 GMT), with the greenback again below Y111, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  apparently gave it another go. \par \par \uc2  The dollar ended Tokyo trading Y2.28 higher at Y112.48-Y112.53. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  shows the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  will not tolerate the dollar's fall below Y110," said a strategist at one leading city bank. \par \par \uc2  Finance Minister Kiichi Miyazawa said he is keeping a close eye on recent yen fluctuations, which he warned are "sharp and disturbing to the market." \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 12-01-99 \par \par \uc2  1401GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv1c008nc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
