\par\par \b \uc2  BOJ  \highlight22\uc2 Intervenes \highlight\uc2  In Mkt, Signaling Yen Has Rallied Enough \b0\par\par\uc2  By Brian Fowler \par \uc2 286 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Januar 1999\par 10:42\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO (Dow Jones)--The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to support the dollar Tuesday, triggering a wave of short-covering buying that helped drive the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  up four yen from the start of the day. \par \par \uc2  Coming after the dollar touched a 28-month low in New York Monday, the action sent a strong signal to the market that Japan believes the yen's 36% surge against the dollar since last August has gone far enough. \par \par \uc2  A Japanese monetary official confirmed late in the Tokyo day that the BOJ sold a relatively small amount of yen - less than $1.0 billion - to purchase dollars. Speaking to Dow Jones on condition of anonymity, the official said: "The Bank of Japan bought dollars for yen in the Tuesday morning session. The volume of buying was less than $1 billion." \par \par \uc2  The official didn't disclose the level at which the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but many market participants said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  appeared to have entered the market around Y109.00. As the dollar rose, traders scrambled to cover short positions, pushing the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  through several key layers of resistance. \par \par \uc2  By the end of the Asian day, the dollar had risen to Y112.78, well up from Y108.72 in New York late Monday and from Y108.70 at the start of the Asian day. \par \par \uc2  The dollar fell to Y108.21 in New York Monday, touching its lowest level since August 1996 and marking a 36% rise in the yen since the dollar hit an eight-year high of Y147.61 in August. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 12-01-99 \par \par \uc2  0942GMT \par \par \uc2  1137 4202 55127 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv1c00894\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
