\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2  Official-2: BOJ Seen To Have  \highlight22\uc2 Intervened \highlight\uc2  Around Y109 \b0\par\par\uc2 131 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Januar 1999\par 08:16\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO (Dow Jones)--A Japanese monetary official said Tuesday that the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market during the morning, buying dollars against the yen. \par \par \uc2  Speaking to Dow Jones on condition of anonymity, the official said: "The Bank of Japan bought dollars for yen in the Tuesday morning session. The volume of buying was less than $1 billion." The official didn't disclose the level at which the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The dollar surged almost three yen to above Y111.00 during the Asian morning, with the rise fueled in part by rumors the BOJ had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Several traders said the BOJ conducted waves of dollar-yen buying around Y109.00. \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 12-01-99 \par \par \uc2  0716GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv1c007u4\par }\par \b \uc2 Zusammenfassung der Suche\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Text\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 (foreign exchange or fx or forex or currenc*) and (interven* or operation*) and (japan near10 interven*) and (rst=trtw or rst=tprw or rst=tdjw) and (central bank or ministry of finance or treasury ministry or monetary authority)\cell \pard